# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the nightly asan-ubsan job (docs/Testing.md#third-party-code).
# Only allocations third-party code keeps on purpose; name the library and why.

# SDL3 keeps a per-thread error buffer (SDL_SetError) for threads it didn't create, such as
# the job workers that load WAV files; it is freed only by SDL_CleanupTLS on that thread.
leak:SDL_GetErrBuf

# SDL3's X11 backend keeps a few allocations from its video init past SDL_Quit (the X
# resource database in X11_GetGlobalContentScale, the locale copy in X11_InitIM); seen
# under Xvfb. Shockwave calls SDL_Quit; nothing of ours runs under X11_VideoInit.
leak:X11_VideoInit

# libdbus (a system library SDL3 starts for desktop services) keeps buffers it read for the
# life of the process, by design.
leak:libdbus-1.so
